* brew tap bbc/audiowaveform
* brew install audiowaveform
* brew install ffmpeg aubio
* bundle
* update PLAYLIST_ID in server.rb
* rake

At startup, the server queues every track in PLAYLIST_ID for WAV conversion,
waveform generation and BPM/beat-grid analysis. One background worker processes
the queue; opening a track or requesting one of its analysis files moves it to
the front of the waiting queue. Work already in progress finishes first.

Audio, waveforms and beat grids are cached by Music's persistent track ID and
reused across restarts and tag/path changes. New files are published atomically,
so interrupted work is retried rather than served as a completed result.

The playlist refreshes every 60 seconds in a separate background thread. Set
PLAYLIST_REFRESH_INTERVAL to change the interval in seconds. Refreshes queue new
tracks, retry failures, update track descriptions and delete cached audio,
waveforms, beat grids and artwork for removed tracks. An active removed track
is cleaned up when its current work finishes. If Music cannot be read, the
previous playlist and caches are kept until a successful refresh.

Saving the track form immediately updates the cached title/artist description
used by the main view and status endpoint, without rerunning audio analysis.

GET /api/status reports per-track stages, available artifacts, detected BPM,
queue order, errors and playlist refresh time. The main view polls it every
three seconds to show analysis progress and playlist changes. Analysis file
requests return 503 on failure or after a five-minute wait (with Retry-After),
and 404 for tracks outside the playlist.

Run the tests with rake test.
